      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T01:26:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this properly generalised? Looking at my laptop:\n\n\n```\n$ ls /sys/bus/usb/devices/1-0:1.0@   3-1:1.0@  3-4:1.2@    3-5.3:1.0@    3-6.2.1:1.1@  3-6.4.2@\n2-0:1.0@   3-1:1.1@  3-4:1.3@    3-6@          3-6.2.1:1.2@  3-6.4.2.1@\n2-1@       3-1:1.2@  3-4:1.4@    3-6.1@        3-6.2.1:1.3@  3-6.4.2:1.0@\n2-1:1.0@   3-1:1.3@  3-5@        3-6:1.0@      3-6.2.1:1.4@  3-6.4.2.1:1.0@\n3-0:1.0@   3-3@      3-5:1.0@    3-6.1:1.0@    3-6.2.1:1.5@  4-0:1.0@\n3-1@       3-3:1.0@  3-5.2@      3-6.2@        3-6.3@        usb1@\n3-10@      3-4@      3-5.2:1.0@  3-6.2.1@      3-6.3:1.0@    usb2@\n3-10:1.0@  3-4:1.0@  3-5.2:1.1@  3-6.2:1.0@    3-6.4@        usb3@\n3-10:1.1@  3-4:1.1@  3-5.3@      3-6.2.1:1.0@  3-6.4:1.0@    usb4@\n\n```\n\nInspecting `3-6`, because it seems interesting wrt to the question:\n\n```\n$ ls -1d /sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/*/\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/3-6.1//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/3-6:1.0//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/3-6.2//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/3-6.3//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/3-6.4//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/driver//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/ep_00//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/firmware_node//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/physical_location//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/port//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/power//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/subsystem//\n/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/typec//\n\n```\n\nIf `port` has multiple elements, then I don\u0027t think this works. However, the \"top-level\" `/sys/bus/usb/devices/` symlinks appear to traverse the nesting that\u0027s present under `/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6/`:\n\n```\n$ realpath \u0027/sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6.2.1:1.0\u0027\n/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:14.0/usb3/3-6/3-6.2/3-6.2.1/3-6.2.1:1.0\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 649,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 649,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "02c878b2e5f3b8ebb90a12ef5c5a59c021b63c0d",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
